Consolidated R&D and MG&A Expenses
Total R&D and MG&A expenses for Q3 2025 were $4.4 billion, down 20% from Q3 2024, and $14.0 billion for YTD 2025, down 17% from YTD 2024. These expenses represent 31.9% of revenue for Q3 2025 and 40.9% of revenue for Q3 2024, and 35.7% of revenue for YTD 2025 and 43.6% of revenue for YTD 2024.In support of our strategy, described in our 2024 Form 10-K, we continue to make investments to advance our process technology roadmap. As a result of our 2025 Restructuring Plan, 2024 Restructuring Plan, and related cost-reduction measures, we expect a decrease in total R&D and MG&A expenses in 2025 relative to recent historical periods as we focus investments in R&D and create capacity for sustained investment in technology and manufacturing. Research and Development $B
