‚Ä¢
If we lose Microsoft Corporation‚Äôs support for our products or other software vendors do not design and develop software to run on our products, our ability to sell our products could be materially adversely affected. ‚Ä¢
Our reliance on third-party distributors and add-in-board (AIB) partners subjects us to certain risks. ‚Ä¢
Our business depends on the proper functioning of our internal business processes and information systems. ‚Ä¢
Our products may not be compatible with some or all industry-standard software and hardware. ‚Ä¢
Costs related to defective products could have a material adverse effect on us. ‚Ä¢
We may fail to maintain the efficiency of our supply chain as we respond to changes in customer demand. ‚Ä¢
We outsource to third parties certain supply-chain logistics functions. ‚Ä¢
We may be unable to effectively control the sales of our products on the gray market. ‚Ä¢
Climate change may have an impact on our business. Legal and Regulatory Risks
‚Ä¢
Government actions and regulations, including but not limited to export regulations, import tariffs and trade protection measures, may limit our ability to export our products to certain customers. ‚Ä¢
If we cannot realize our deferred tax assets, our results of operations could be adversely affected. ‚Ä¢
Our business is subject to potential tax liabilities, including as a result of tax regulation changes. ‚Ä¢
We are party to litigation and may become a party to other claims or litigation.‚Ä¢
We are subject to environmental laws, conflict minerals regulations, as well as a variety of other laws or regulations. ‚Ä¢
Evolving expectations from governments, investors, customers and other stakeholders regarding corporate responsibility matters could result in additional costs, harm to our reputation and a loss of customers. ‚Ä¢
Issues related to the responsible use of AI may result in reputational, competitive and financial harm and liability. ‚Ä¢
The agreements governing our notes, our guarantee of Xilinx‚Äôs notes and the Revolving Credit Agreement. Merger, Acquisition, Divestiture, and Integration Risks
‚Ä¢
Acquisitions, joint ventures, and/or strategic investments, and the failure to integrate acquired businesses may fail to materialize their anticipated benefits and could disrupt our business. ‚Ä¢
Any impairment of our tangible, definite-lived intangible or indefinite-lived intangible assets, including goodwill, may adversely impact our financial position and results of operations. General Risks
‚Ä¢
Our worldwide operations are subject to political, legal and economic risks and natural disasters. ‚Ä¢
We may incur future impairments of our technology license purchases. ‚Ä¢
Our inability to continue to attract and retain key employees may hinder our business. ‚Ä¢
