The valuation techniques used to measure the fair values of the Company‚Äôs Level 2 financial instruments, which generally have counterparties with high credit ratings, are based on quoted market prices or model-driven valuations using significant inputs derived from or corroborated by observable market data. As of December¬†27, 2025, 
78
% of the Company‚Äôs non-current marketable debt securities other than mortgage- and asset-backed securities had maturities between 1 and 5 years, 
